\name{cellucid_history_squash}
\alias{cellucid_history_squash}
\title{Merge steps into one}
\usage{
cellucid_history_squash(viewer, from, to)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{from}{The first step to merge. Text. Required.}
\item{to}{The last step to merge. Text. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{groups_removed} (Groups that held only these steps, removed with them), \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{journal} (Its Recently deleted entry), \code{squashed} (Steps it replaced), \code{step} (The squashed step).
}
\description{
Replace consecutive steps of one branch (from first to last, whole turns; a group's are its steps) with one squashed step from the first one's state to the last one's; elsewhere it replays as values only. Refused when another branch starts inside; the steps go to Recently deleted. An agent squashes only its own turn's steps.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.squash} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_squash(viewer, from = "s4",
      to = "s9")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
